WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.830
Speaker 1: As if we needed any more confirmation
that Madison Cawthorn being kicked out of

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:09.230
the House of Representatives after just one
term is a very, very good thing.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:15.700
I'm going to present to you today exhibit
number 150 of why Cawthorn using his final

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:25.539
speaking opportunity on the floor of the House
to rail against and I quote here, soft metrosexuals.

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:27.140
Take a look at this clip.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:34.250
This is a guy who seems obsessed with gender
stuff and even cultural issues that aren't

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:35.250
big issues.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.830
Now, I think it's been 12 years since I heard
the term metrosexual, because here is Madison

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:44.920
Cawthorn delivering this final principled
and defiant speech on the floor of the House

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:45.920
of Representatives.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.681
Speaker 2: Our young men are taught that weakness
is strength, that delicacy is desirable, and

00:00:50.681 --> 00:00:56.110
that being a soft metrosexual is more valuable
than training the mind, body and soul.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.469
Social media has weakened us, stifling our
men of their will to fight, to rise in a noble

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:04.850
manner, square their jaws in charge once more
to the breach of life to defend what they

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.299
love.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:10.420
So on this precipice of disaster, I. Ask the
young men of this nation a question Will you

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.159
sit behind a screen while the story tales
of your forefathers become myth, or you stand

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:18.430
resolute against the dying light of America's
golden age?

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.439
We reclaim your masculinity.

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:24.670
Will you become a man to be feared, to be
respected, to be looked up to?

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.610
Or you let this nation's next generation be
its final generation?

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:33.079
Speaker 1: That line about Will you become
a man to be feared?

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:34.479
You know.

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:43.460
Call me crazy, but I respect people who garner
respect, not who make others afraid.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:50.000
And in fact, often those who make others afraid
are quite cowardly people when it really comes

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.000
down to it.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.229
And this is really, you know, it's easy to
say, oh, it's Madison Cawthorn with another

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:58.710
one of his wacky rants on his way out.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:02.189
Don't let the door hit you as you as you exit
sort of thing.

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:08.289
But he brings up an idea or a concept that
is becoming increasingly common among the

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:14.569
right, which is that fear is they just love
fear in every sense.

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:20.310
They they see those who are feared as powerful
and to be respected.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.230
They use fear based politics and fear mongering
to get people to vote for them.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:29.180
Oh, the you've got to be afraid of the violent
immigrants that are coming in and you've got

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.200
to be afraid of the crazy communists that
have taken over Congress.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.390
And of course, none of these things are true.

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:36.860
Fear is a big part of their politics.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:40.940
And Madison Cawthorn just explaining an additional
way in which that's the case.

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.530
Now, as far as the metrosexual stuff, I don't
know that I've heard anyone complain about

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.110
metrosexual since 2008.

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:51.400
Like, yeah, very, very, very early in 2008,
I would even say.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.209
And for people who maybe don't remember or
never knew what that term meant, metrosexual

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:05.450
referred to a young, often urban heterosexual
male.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.930
Often with left leaning political views.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:15.900
Who's interested in fashion and has what might
be considered a refined sense of taste?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:24.500
And it was a way of criticizing heterosexuals
who you can't just say, Oh, they're gay by

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:30.160
saying this is a brand of heterosexuality
that is sort of less manly and less masculine.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.970
Again, I haven't heard metrosexual as a term
used in a very, very long time, but we clearly

00:03:35.970 --> 00:04:51.050
know what is on Madison Catherine's mind.

